WEBVTT

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.480
night or

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.540
The city is London.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:28.200
Down to see the queen.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.520
Good morning, Duchess.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:37.570
Three days and nights. No word.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:39.540
I love you, Duchess.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.720
And if anybody says I love you just for your title...

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.860
Three days and nights.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.580
Busy man in a busy town.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.500
Thinking the horrible thoughts.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.290
Seeing you lifeless in the gutter.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.390
Oh, you should have caviar for breakfast.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.490
Oh, hiding in some cellar, running for your life.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:55.930
Running? Me?

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.960
Harry Fabian never runs for me.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.090
Harry, you're not in trouble again, are you?

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:11.810
Trouble? Here, look at this. What do you see?

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.110
Why, it's a pill. That's right, it's a pill.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:26.810
Now watch, Mary, watch. One pill. One pill the size of a baby's fingernail.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.640
Drop into the tank of your motor car, it triples your mileage.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:35.200
Fabian's fume fee. A box of 12 for half a crown takes you 12 times around the town.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.240
But where'd you get it, Al?

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.760
Little Al, the six-penny chemist in Whitechapel.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.620
But does he know what he's got? No, no head for business.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.020
I'll just lock him away in an attic with his chemicals turning out pills by the tongue.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:47.340
You mean you want to back this?

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.180
Well, that's what I want to talk to you about.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.380
From here on, Duchess, it's a life of ease and plenty for you.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.040
Now, all I need is 300 pounds to develop... No.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.970
But it's the biggest thing I've ever found.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:01.150
No.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.600
I've got it right here in the palm of my hand.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.260
No.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:07.100
For 300 quid, we can package 5,000 boxes.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:07.420
No.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.340
Sell over half a crown.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.000
That's a profit of over 100...

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:14.790
You've got the money.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:17.860
You know you've got it.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.530
You've got it right here.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:22.500
Yes.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.360
Yes, I've got it.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.620
Put it by, shilling after shilling.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.240
But not for this.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.840
Not for mad get-rich-quick scheme.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.690
The money's there for the day you come to your senses.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:38.900
Settle down to, no matter what, a grocery's, a tobacco shop,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.460
anything done in the light of day.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.220
Listen, Mary, I...

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.290
Harry, do you think I enjoy slaving night after night in a silver fox?

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:48.640
Getting drunk's drunker. I'm sticking it out.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.600
Waiting for the day we can marry, lead decent, normal lives.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.620
I know, I know, darling.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.760
That's what the money's for, and until then, we don't touch one penny of it.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.870
You don't understand, Mary. This is our big chance.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.870
Big chance? Oh, again?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:06.940
Last month, the Fabian Mail Order Company couldn't lose, but we lost 50 of the best.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.380
Before that, the Fabian Tourist Bureau, the Fabian Song Publishers.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.100
What wasn't I going to have?

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.930
The Royal Suite on the Queen Mary, a house in Mayfair.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.930
But this is different. It's a sure thing.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.390
It's always different. Now the Fabian Fuel Feeder.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.730
A fortune with every pill.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.430
Yes, a fortune. Two fortunes.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.400
That's what I want and that's what I'll get.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.220
I'm through with mugs and spivs and dirt.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:29.980
One break, I'm out of the gum.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.220
Garbage cans for life. I'm in the higher brackets. A mister with a future.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:36.060
There he goes. They'll say, that's Fabian. That's Harry Fabian.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.320
One break, I'm hot as a rocket shooting diamonds for sparks.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:48.400
Harry! Oh, Harry. Harry, duh.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:55.860
I want to be something.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:05.970
You're so unhappy. Always running, always in a sweat.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.890
Harry, remember them. Nice people.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.900
Nice to know and be with.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.680
Remember the plans they used to make?

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.980
The kind of life they were going to live?

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:29.310
Oh, Harry, how did we ever lose track of them?

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:36.840
It wasn't so very long ago, not more than a million years ago.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.930
Don't you see, it isn't important just to be somebody.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:48.980
The important thing is to be with somebody.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:54.170
Someone who wants nothing better than to live and work by your side.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:58.340
Quiet. Peace.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.120
Oh, Harry, please.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.880
It's getting late. Noceros is angry.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:21.260
Hang Noceros and the Silver Fox. I'm not going.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.840
You mean you're afraid to go into the street?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.420
What do you mean I'm afraid? I'm not afraid of anything.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:39.790
Made him a partner. Ten percent slice of the profits, but five pounds.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.040
Five measly quid to pay little Alf for his chemicals.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.690
Now the welcher wants his money back.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.450
Five pounds for those pills.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:57.510
No business, head little Alf. Wait here.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.020
Yes, with the usual disastrous results.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.400
Mary, get that siphon bottle there quickly.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:25.540
Hurry, hurry.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.130
Don't just stand there, woman. Squirt, squirt.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:40.360
There. You're just in time to enjoy the most heavenly spaghetti dinner.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.380
Ah, thanks. But I've just had breakfast, unfortunately.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.540
I admit it does look a little overdone.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.830
Oh, well. Try again next week.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.950
Probably starve doing it, but I'll master it in the end, I promise.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.410
That's the thing that keeps us apart, you know.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:56.390
Your spaghetti?

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:59.970
Yes, in a way. When I'm having my spaghetti, you're looking...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.300
for your morning toast. Do you think we might ever arrange our day to meet somewhere around tea

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:09.520
time? Come on, sit down. Oh, here, let me get these hideous little monsters out of the way. Oh, I think

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:15.320
he's cute. She? Well, she's cute. The shops tell me it's the best-selling design I've given them so

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:21.700
far. Discouraging. You're probably pleased as punch. Of course. Sit down and really be comfortable.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:27.230
Thanks, Adam, but I've got to get on to work. I've come to ask for a favor. Name it. Could you let me

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.510
have three pounds until tomorrow? Help yourself.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.660
Punch the night bell. The old lady of Threadneedle Street is well-stocked and quite generous.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.860
You know, it does look like the Bank of England.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:38.380
Well, it should. I spent half my youth reproducing it.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:40.090
It's very good.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:40.930
Of course.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.200
Wonderful. You're very clever, Adam.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:50.940
I am about unimportant things.

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:53.850
So...

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.360
Thanks, Adam. I happen to need this right now for...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:10:59.970
Well, I didn't expect...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.060
I expect them to deliver the...

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:01.500
Sure.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:05.590
Harry's back.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.240
You knew that, didn't you?

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.140
These walls?

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.010
Just one big happy family.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.210
He gets so excited, almost like a child.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.940
But you know, Adam, one has to fight not to get pulled in by his excitement.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.470
His ideas always have so much imagination.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:22.700
I know.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.800
Harry's an artist without an art.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.160
What does that mean?

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:29.810
Well, that's something that can make a man very unhappy.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.970
groping for the right lever, the means with which to express himself.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:37.600
Yes, he is that, isn't he? I like that, Adam.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:39.620
It's a very nice thought.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.450
Yes, but it can be dangerous.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.190
Oh, no, you don't. Not again.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:46.490
Every time you talk, you mix me up so I can't think straight for a week.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:48.170
Thanks, Adam.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.730
Anything. Anytime.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:11.570
Five pounds by your partner out.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:13.760
Thanks.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.040
Good back to you tonight.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:22.460
See you at the Silver Fox.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:22.840
All right.

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:40.880
Thank you, Maggie. Can't win, boys.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:42.720
What's it?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.320
Howdy!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:44.160
Howdy!

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:45.610
How's that?

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:46.500
Cheers, Harry.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:47.340
Never mind.

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:49.610
When are you going to open up your parents' office?

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:52.660
Evening, Molly.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.240
Evening, Molly.

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:58.970
Well, you're sober. Trade must be slow.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:12:59.730
Slow.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.520
Don't disintegrate in for her. You need a pretty carnation.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.240
Thanks, Molly. Put it on my account, will you?

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.120
That's all right, my dear. I'll trust you.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:07.680
There you are, Bert.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.460
Off a crown.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:10.220
Don't mention it.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:15.660
And if you girls want to work for my husband, you've got to start off on the right foot.

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:19.220
You must understand the rules, what he'll stand for and what he won't.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.920
First, no stealing from the gentleman while you're in the club.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.270
No wages, but generous commissions.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:28.720
Oh, yes, chocolates. Fancy boxes we sell at two pounds.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:29.960
Isn't two quid a bit steep?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.510
They're hand-dipped, dearie.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:37.330
When the night's out, I'll buy them back from you.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:38.610
Evening, Phil.

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:41.920
Need any help with that stuff?

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.490
Where have you been, dear boy?

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:46.120
Well, I've...

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:48.240
Been having a pleasant holiday at Cannes?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.600
Or spending the weekend at Windsor Castle?

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:51.560
I've been ill.

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:54.900
Oh, poor boy's been ill.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:55.800
What a pity.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.260
So you were.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:58.880
I read all about it in the Times.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:13:59.970
Mr. Han...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.340
Mr. Fabian, it's head, is being treated by the court physician.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:08.230
Mr. Fabian, it is reported, is suffering from a highly inflamed imagination.

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.880
A couple by delusions of grandeur.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:12.290
Well, where's he been?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.900
Now, now, now, Helen, mustn't be unkind. The dear boy's been at death's door.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.630
Well, I'm glad to see you're fully recovered.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.350
We were worried about him, weren't we, Phil?

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:22.270
Indeed we were.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:28.200
It's getting late. Time for dear boy to get dressed and hop it.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.380
Take care of yourself, dear boy.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:11.100
Hey, Harry, three live ones, what's it worth to you?

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.640
Depends on how much you know.

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.320
Depends on how much you'll go.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:18.370
From Chicago, men's clothing business.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:23.010
One of them, the half-bite, kept on talking about a friend of his called Lamont he must write to.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:26.750
This here Lamont's in the motor supply business in something he calls the Loop.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.360
Good evening, sir.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:34.940
Good evening.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:35.720
The usual.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:36.460
If you please.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.300
It's good to have you back in London, sir.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.140
Thank you, Charles.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:51.900
I beg your pardon.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.500
Does this wallet belong to one of you gentlemen?

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.360
Why, no, it doesn't.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:56.960
Good evening, Mr. Phoebe.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:57.960
Oh, good evening, Emil.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:15:59.930
Someone must have dropped this.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.700
I'll soon come running for it, no doubt.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:02.760
Thank you, Mr. Peavy.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.120
Happened to me once back in the States,

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.680
traveling from New York to San Francisco.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.560
Changed trains to Chicago, you know.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.930
It would be darned if I don't lose my wallet.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:13.310
No.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.350
Luckily, I knew a chap in the loop, motorcyclized.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.090
A fella named Lamont.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:18.730
Lamont?

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:19.910
Did you say Lamont?

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:20.250
Oh, yes.

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:21.590
You mean Stubby Lamont?

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:22.530
Why, yes.

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:23.730
Well, what do you know, Stubby?

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:26.090
You said, listen, we were just talking about him.

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:26.450
Yeah.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.410
Oh, wait till I tell Stubby.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:29.710
Yes, just wait.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:32.180
It's like meeting someone from home.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:33.320
Yes, it's quite a coincidence.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:34.000
Yes.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:35.860
Have a cigarette.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:36.760
Yes, have a cigarette.

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:38.660
Thank you, gentlemen. Thank you very much.

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:40.840
Have you been in London long?

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:41.620
Just two days.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:43.120
On business?

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:44.120
Well, you know.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.380
Yes, I know.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.040
Well, I'm sure your business will be a great success.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:50.280
Good night, gentlemen.

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:51.470
Good night.

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:52.200
Good night.

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:58.590
Say, you boys surely don't plan to spend the entire evening here.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:16:59.870
Always open to suggestions.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.230
As a matter of fact, I do know of a pleasure.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:04.650
You have?

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.000
It's a bit naughty.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.700
But great fun.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:10.700
Silver Fox, private club.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:12.140
Private club?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:12.580
Mm-hmm.

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.240
Oh, you take my card. You'll be well taken care of.

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:16.520
Why, thanks. That's sweet.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.600
It's a pleasure.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:18.020
Good night.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:19.760
Good night.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.820
When you write to Stubby, give him my best, will you?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:23.920
You bet.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:24.300
Sure.

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:29.460
Good night.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:29.800
Good night.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:34.130
Good night, gentlemen.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:34.910
Good night.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:35.110
Good night.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:35.570
Good night.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:42.300
Pardon me. Does this wallet belong to one of you, gentlemen?

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:44.720
Out.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.280
I beg your pardon.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:47.940
Out.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.850
What do you mean? This is a public place.

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:52.750
So is them all. Move.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:56.190
Evidently, you don't know who I am.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:59.970
Mr. Christo don't like club touts hustling suckers in his...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.500
Get out!

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:02.840
Pigs!

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:04.120
Pigs!

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:05.370
Pigs!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.330
Let them here!

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:08.340
Pigs!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:08.980
Come on!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.270
That's Gregorius!

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:11.830
Who?

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:14.500
Finest wrestler of the world's ever known.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:19.520
Papa, please.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:20.900
Where are you going?

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:24.390
Is it for this you brought me from Athens?

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:26.090
The circus?

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.470
What have you done to wrestling?

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:29.970
Do you think I...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.760
and permit Nicholas to wrestle with such filth?

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.260
No, no, no, no. Take it easy, old boy. Take it easy.

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:38.630
You do not talk like that to my father. Get out.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.320
For this, I do not thank you, my son.

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.760
Please, Papa, listen to me.

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:48.480
You must understand that times have changed.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.570
Tastes, people, everything changes.

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.890
Tomorrow morning, I'll take you and Nicholas to Liverpool.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:54.710
I've got everything arranged for you there.

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:59.710
An arena, a gymnasium. I want to do only good for you, Papa.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.120
I see you have a nice life now, to be near you.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:06.500
Tomorrow, I go back to Athens.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.020
I demand my money.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.700
How dare you call this filthy exhibition rest?

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:37.600
I beg your pardon?

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.140
I demand my money back, do you hear me?

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:41.080
Easy on, easy on. Where's your ticket?

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.020
It's right here.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:44.830
I've never witnessed such a spectacle.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:55.060
No, no, it can't be.

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:57.340
You're not Gregorius.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.300
Gregorius the Great.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.010
See, Nicholas, there are people who do not forget great wrestling.

00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:07.190
Forget? Forget the greatest wrestler the world has ever known?

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:12.900
It's good to see the memory of great, noble wrestling is not dead.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:14.700
I thank you, young man.

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:15.720
I thank you, sir.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:17.290
My name is Harry Faber.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:19.420
This is Nicholas.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:20.560
A fine-looking lad.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:21.200
Thanks.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:26.320
You suppose you could pin a man like the Strangler, say?

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:27.560
Yes.

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:28.270
Oh.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:36.260
Nicholas pinned ten stranglers, all in same ring, same time.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:40.140
Well, well, yes, I should think he could.

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:44.480
I would consider it a great honor, sir, if you and Nicholas would have a drink with me.

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:48.160
Forgive me, young man. Tonight I am not good company.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:50.860
We must go to hotel and pack.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.860
Oh, just for one drink. There's a little pub right across the street.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.760
Young man, you are too charming.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.500
Very well, young man.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:21:59.500
Fine, fine.

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:05.620
You know, I have a strange feeling that our meeting tonight is, uh...

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:07.220
Well, we'll talk over our drinks.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:21.720
Raise your elbow to champagne.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:23.990
Empty your glass.

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:28.900
Fill it to the fresh new new.

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:33.250
What to do with the grapes that he grew?

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:38.640
Here's to the sun, ripening the vine.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:42.660
Here's to the bottles, holding the wine.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:51.640
Drink it all tomorrow.

00:23:04.890 --> 00:23:05.070
You

00:23:30.670 --> 00:23:31.930
The song went well tonight, didn't it?

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:46.860
Yes. Good idea of yours, that song.

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:57.190
Thank you, darling, those Americans.

00:23:57.740 --> 00:23:59.480
Spending as if tonight was their last on Earth.

00:24:01.690 --> 00:24:03.810
Harry Fabian's still the best hustler in the business.

00:24:04.110 --> 00:24:05.170
That is, my love.

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:10.410
Oh, you needn't worry. Five quid won't take me far on the silver fox.

00:24:10.650 --> 00:24:12.290
Now, now, now, Pets.

00:24:13.250 --> 00:24:15.050
You know you can have anything you want.

00:24:15.210 --> 00:24:16.070
Anything but money.

00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:20.100
Fur coats, perfumes, good food and wines.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:21.970
What would you need money for?

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.570
A bit of independence. Try and buy me some of that.

00:24:29.530 --> 00:24:29.970
Something...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.860
really lovely for you in there, precious.

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:34.240
Has it been taken off for stolen property in this chip?

00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:36.760
I'll bet you know I wouldn't let you

00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:38.640
wear anything while it was still

00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:49.020
hot. Like it, my love?

00:24:51.350 --> 00:24:53.730
Yes, it's nice. Thank you, Phil.

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:56.300
I've long thought it appropriate that

00:24:56.300 --> 00:24:58.660
the wife of the owner of the Silver Fox

00:24:58.660 --> 00:24:59.960
should wear

00:25:01.160 --> 00:25:07.090
I've hit it. I've hit it. I've hit it. I've hit it. I've hit it. Hundreds, thousands of fortunes, Fabian promotions. I've hit it, Phil.

00:25:07.410 --> 00:25:08.910
Now, now, now. What's all this?

00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:10.990
Wrestling. All-in wrestling.

00:25:11.210 --> 00:25:11.790
Hey, hey.

00:25:11.990 --> 00:25:16.650
Phil, I hold here in the palm of my hand the means to control wrestling in all London.

00:25:16.990 --> 00:25:17.950
Control wrestling?

00:25:18.250 --> 00:25:19.730
In all London.

00:25:20.210 --> 00:25:20.490
You?

00:25:20.870 --> 00:25:21.150
Me.

00:25:22.030 --> 00:25:25.820
Dear fellow, have you ever heard of a citizen called Crystal?

00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:29.480
Ha, ha! Know what I got in here, Phil? Huh? Crystal!

00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:41.160
Oh, no. No, no, Phil, you don't understand. I've got Christo. I've got Christo where I want him. Gregorius, see? I've got Gregorius.

00:25:41.280 --> 00:25:44.560
Oh, dear boy. Dear boy, you'll be the death of me.

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:57.340
Listen, Phil, hear me out. I've got Christo stopped. Gregorius, Christo's his son, don't you see? He's my shield, see? He won't raise a hand to his father. Gregorius will protect me from Christo, Phil, see? I only need a few hundred...

00:25:57.340 --> 00:25:58.860
Just listen to me!

00:25:59.120 --> 00:25:59.980
You give me...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.740
I'll make you a rich man!

00:26:01.900 --> 00:26:03.100
Make me a rich man!

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:03.700
Throw him up!

00:26:04.740 --> 00:26:06.260
Oh, no!

00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:09.380
Must be unkind to the dear boy.

00:26:09.740 --> 00:26:11.220
I haven't laughed so much.

00:26:12.670 --> 00:26:16.330
You big businessman, Mr. Financial Wizard.

00:26:16.490 --> 00:26:19.070
Do you know what it means to earn 400 quid?

00:26:19.370 --> 00:26:20.450
Let me see you.

00:26:20.730 --> 00:26:21.070
Get him.

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:22.420
Get 300.

00:26:23.160 --> 00:26:23.460
200.

00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:27.940
Yes, why don't you get 200 of your own and put it on that desk?

00:26:28.160 --> 00:26:29.700
My husband won't match it.

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:33.040
Oh, that's right. You put 200 here.

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:34.100
All right, get it.

00:26:34.870 --> 00:26:36.510
Twice three times 400.

00:26:36.670 --> 00:26:37.930
Now flick it in your face.

00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:42.480
Go on, let yourself to pieces.

00:26:43.650 --> 00:26:44.250
I'll show you.

00:26:44.450 --> 00:26:46.400
I'll show everybody.

00:26:47.060 --> 00:26:48.840
I'll be back with 200 new matches.

00:26:49.240 --> 00:26:50.400
I'll show you.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.620
Harry, all I got is me money.

00:27:02.150 --> 00:27:04.290
And between me and me money is a kind of understanding.

00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:06.000
Like only matrimony.

00:27:06.430 --> 00:27:07.490
Do death us do part.

00:27:07.550 --> 00:27:08.810
But I can't miss Vigler.

00:27:09.430 --> 00:27:09.830
Harry.

00:27:09.930 --> 00:27:10.850
Vigler, will you listen?

00:27:11.850 --> 00:27:12.990
I like you, Harry.

00:27:13.910 --> 00:27:14.970
Why did you settle down?

00:27:15.620 --> 00:27:17.920
Get hold of a few good beggars and put them out on the street.

00:27:18.430 --> 00:27:19.790
I'll give you all the supplies you need.

00:27:19.890 --> 00:27:21.290
Legs, eyes, stumps.

00:27:21.470 --> 00:27:22.230
What are you talking about?

00:27:22.230 --> 00:27:24.070
You can make a nice living out of it, Harry.

00:27:24.380 --> 00:27:24.660
Hmm?

00:27:25.430 --> 00:27:26.970
I bring you a fortune.

00:27:26.970 --> 00:27:28.490
You give me beggars.

00:27:31.180 --> 00:27:33.420
And if I had the money, I could help you, couldn't I?

00:27:34.100 --> 00:27:37.880
Right. And if I could help you, I would, wouldn't I?

00:27:38.580 --> 00:27:42.800
Right. But if you ain't got socks, you can't pull them up, now, can you?

00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:44.680
Oh, now, Guggan, you're a man of imagination.

00:27:44.680 --> 00:27:45.840
I'm with all the best will in the world.

00:27:45.980 --> 00:27:49.200
I'm just helpless. Just plain sprawling helpless.

00:27:49.420 --> 00:27:52.580
This is a golden opportunity, Guggan. One chance in a thousand.

00:27:53.540 --> 00:27:55.360
Invest your money where it means something.

00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:57.400
I'm just plain simple sorry, Harry.

00:27:57.980 --> 00:27:59.520
But if you want anything else...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.250
I can print you a passport, birth certificate, medical license.

00:28:04.550 --> 00:28:07.110
Just ask old Gugin and it's yours.

00:28:09.460 --> 00:28:11.000
And that's how it is, Harry.

00:28:11.220 --> 00:28:13.200
But, Anna, listen, I can give you everything...

00:28:13.200 --> 00:28:14.220
You're wasting your time and mine.

00:28:14.420 --> 00:28:16.540
Anna O'Leary's got only one business.

00:28:17.200 --> 00:28:18.440
Balance of the nylons.

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:20.980
Good. I could do with another 50,000 cigarettes.

00:28:21.260 --> 00:28:24.680
Ah, cigarette stockings. This is big, Anna.

00:28:24.760 --> 00:28:28.740
One business. And that don't call for me putting 200 quid into another man's game.

00:28:28.860 --> 00:28:29.980
But it's the chance of a life.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.300
Anna O'Leary don't take no chances.

00:28:32.460 --> 00:28:34.100
I'm a hard-working, hard-headed businesswoman.

00:28:34.740 --> 00:28:38.120
Oh, now, look, you don't want to spend the rest of your life living like this, do you?

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:40.740
Shady deals hiding on the river.

00:28:41.020 --> 00:28:43.860
You can live with me, Anna. It's a life of ease and plenty.

00:28:44.550 --> 00:28:46.650
I'm taking great pleasure in bidding you. Good night.

00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:01.240
Is that you, Helen?

00:29:02.410 --> 00:29:04.840
No, it's me, Mary.

00:29:06.660 --> 00:29:14.320
Why don't you go home, Mary?

00:29:15.100 --> 00:29:17.120
Oh, I'm just waiting for Harry, Mr. Nothra.

00:29:18.010 --> 00:29:19.050
He'll be along soon.

00:29:22.960 --> 00:29:25.160
Helen must have slipped out for a breath of air.

00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:27.540
She's got a slight headache.

00:29:29.070 --> 00:29:29.970
Harry's probably still...

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.040
No stopping Harry once he gets started.

00:29:35.170 --> 00:29:35.810
Hello, Molly.

00:29:36.170 --> 00:29:36.770
Hello, Mary.

00:29:37.230 --> 00:29:39.860
Time for a little nourishment.

00:29:42.120 --> 00:29:42.720
Mr. Nostris.

00:29:43.540 --> 00:29:44.360
Yes, Mary?

00:29:45.390 --> 00:29:47.470
Perhaps it's best if I do go on home.

00:29:48.440 --> 00:29:50.040
Would you please tell Harry when he comes?

00:29:51.480 --> 00:29:51.980
Very well.

00:29:53.090 --> 00:29:54.710
I'll tell Harry when he comes.

00:29:55.810 --> 00:29:56.910
Good night, Mr. Nostris.

00:29:57.860 --> 00:29:58.700
Good night, Mary.

00:29:59.370 --> 00:29:59.710
Good night.

00:30:01.470 --> 00:30:07.870
Madam, what a remarkable coincidence.

00:30:08.510 --> 00:30:10.970
All coincidences are, especially this one.

00:30:11.540 --> 00:30:13.220
I was here two hours preparing it.

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:15.760
Are you going home alone?

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:17.140
Oh, no more.

00:30:17.990 --> 00:30:19.450
I just came out here to wait for Harry.

00:30:19.870 --> 00:30:20.850
He'll be long any minute.

00:30:21.280 --> 00:30:22.000
Yes, of course.

00:30:23.840 --> 00:30:24.660
Yes, of course.

00:30:26.060 --> 00:30:27.220
He calls for me every night.

00:30:28.260 --> 00:30:29.660
Just that he's been very busy tonight.

00:30:31.600 --> 00:30:34.160
He's had a lot of parties. He's been working hard.

00:30:34.440 --> 00:30:35.240
Yes, I know.

00:30:39.420 --> 00:30:40.280
Don't be smart.

00:30:41.100 --> 00:30:42.920
You weren't going to wait for Harry, and you know it.

00:30:43.020 --> 00:30:43.920
You were going home alone.

00:30:44.660 --> 00:30:45.440
What if I were?

00:30:46.160 --> 00:30:47.740
If Harry's not here, he's got a good reason.

00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:49.140
Well, that I'm sure of.

00:30:49.680 --> 00:30:51.880
Look, Adam, I don't like you talking down your nose about Harry.

00:30:51.940 --> 00:30:52.580
You don't know him.

00:30:52.660 --> 00:30:52.860
No.

00:30:53.060 --> 00:30:54.520
It's all right for you. You're secure.

00:30:54.700 --> 00:30:55.540
You know where you're going.

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:57.400
Harry's had none of the things you've had.

00:30:57.640 --> 00:30:59.240
Home, education, friends.

00:30:59.620 --> 00:30:59.980
He's...

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.420
He's been on his own ever since he was a kid.

00:31:01.780 --> 00:31:03.960
And he's fighting the only way he knows to keep his head up.

00:31:04.160 --> 00:31:07.040
If he's hurt me, it's because he's been hurt.

00:31:07.140 --> 00:31:07.440
Mary.

00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:09.220
But he's kind at him and generous.

00:31:09.440 --> 00:31:19.980
I know, I was alone in London with no one, nothing but him.

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:30.510
Please, dear.

00:31:36.450 --> 00:31:38.390
Now there's a book that's been looking for you, Harry.

00:31:38.710 --> 00:31:39.850
Tell him to drop dead.

00:31:40.530 --> 00:31:41.070
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:31:59.560 --> 00:31:59.960
You shall drink.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:03.850
Here, Harry. Gin.

00:32:09.580 --> 00:32:10.700
How's the trade, Big Rick?

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:19.880
No, I don't want a life of ease and plenty.

00:32:20.390 --> 00:32:23.190
Take your drink. Drink it quietly.

00:32:24.520 --> 00:32:26.220
Don't mess up with my customers.

00:32:26.660 --> 00:32:28.500
Look at Big Rick. Now look here, Harry.

00:32:45.450 --> 00:32:56.020
thank you thank you very much for slicing my throat playing the loving wife looking out for

00:32:56.020 --> 00:32:59.500
her husband's interest well you don't fool harry fabian

00:33:00.090 --> 00:33:03.030
I know every twist and turn in your scheming brain.

00:33:03.270 --> 00:33:05.150
Oh, yes, and watching every penny just so...

00:33:06.230 --> 00:33:07.250
What do you think you're doing?

00:33:08.190 --> 00:33:08.910
How's Mary?

00:33:08.990 --> 00:33:11.230
You leave Mary alone, do you hear? She's fine with me.

00:33:11.330 --> 00:33:13.190
You married the boss, didn't you? You went on and up.

00:33:13.430 --> 00:33:14.450
But I think of you.

00:33:14.630 --> 00:33:16.210
Yeah, you certainly showed it tonight.

00:33:16.390 --> 00:33:19.450
Put 200 on that desk. My husband'll match it.

00:33:19.650 --> 00:33:23.060
Thank you, Mrs. Nosseris. No. Good night.

00:33:24.340 --> 00:33:28.260
Harry, 200 quid.

00:33:32.080 --> 00:33:33.780
Now, take it to Phil and get his.

00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:37.580
Helen, he never let you have a shilling. Where'd you get it?

00:33:37.660 --> 00:33:39.740
Never mind. Just listen closely and do as I tell you.

00:33:39.800 --> 00:33:41.920
Yeah, sure, Helen. Anything you say, anything you say.

00:33:42.080 --> 00:33:43.080
You show that to Phil.

00:33:43.220 --> 00:33:45.360
He'll give you the 200 quid that I made him promise you.

00:33:48.140 --> 00:33:51.620
When you're a wonder and no mistake, and you won't regret this, I promise you.

00:33:51.780 --> 00:33:52.560
I promise you, Dad.

00:33:53.720 --> 00:33:54.720
Fabian promotions.

00:33:55.560 --> 00:33:56.620
Fabian wrestling will be the...

00:33:56.620 --> 00:33:57.140
There'll be no wrestling.

00:33:57.440 --> 00:33:57.560
What?

00:33:58.080 --> 00:33:58.860
I've got a nightclub.

00:33:59.670 --> 00:33:59.870
Yes.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.220
My own. Bought a year ago. Flamenco's old club.

00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:06.100
Flamenco's closed down. Struck off by the police for two years.

00:34:06.460 --> 00:34:07.300
That's why I got it on credit.

00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:11.260
In another year, all I have to do is to put up five shillings for a license and I'm in business.

00:34:14.560 --> 00:34:16.580
That's what the money's for, a license.

00:34:17.480 --> 00:34:19.120
And you're the only man I know who can get it.

00:34:19.410 --> 00:34:22.570
Oh, but listen, Helen, if Phil gives me the 200, it's got to be for the wrestling.

00:34:22.790 --> 00:34:26.380
That's right. But you'll just go through the motions till we're ready to open the pub.

00:34:26.540 --> 00:34:27.840
But Phil's no easy mark.

00:34:28.080 --> 00:34:28.520
I know.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.340
You're crazy, Alan. You don't know what I've got.

00:34:32.980 --> 00:34:36.020
I've got Gregorius, a shield. I've got Christostak, Coles.

00:34:36.160 --> 00:34:37.820
I can control wrestling in London.

00:34:38.300 --> 00:34:41.340
I'm through hustling for nightclubs for you or for anybody else.

00:34:41.520 --> 00:34:44.080
For yourself. What do you think Phil takes in an evening?

00:34:44.200 --> 00:34:45.400
Never less than a hundred quid.

00:34:45.620 --> 00:34:47.900
And who do you think runs the place for him? I do. Me.

00:34:48.280 --> 00:34:49.920
I know how to make a club spin.

00:34:54.460 --> 00:34:56.120
We're looking for a Mr. Harry Fabian.

00:34:56.480 --> 00:34:58.880
He's not here. The place is closed. Go away.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:00.820
Christos sent us.

00:35:02.830 --> 00:35:03.790
Sorry, forgive me.

00:35:03.850 --> 00:35:06.470
It is I who must ask you to forgive this intrusion, sir.

00:35:07.070 --> 00:35:10.270
But it is imperative that I have a few words with Mr. Harry Fabian.

00:35:10.570 --> 00:35:13.270
I understand he is employed by you, sir.

00:35:13.760 --> 00:35:15.160
Well, in a manner of speaking.

00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:17.300
He works on commission, but I should hardly...

00:35:17.300 --> 00:35:19.310
Yes, quite. My name, sir, is Chilk.

00:35:19.660 --> 00:35:20.360
Fergus Chilk.

00:35:20.780 --> 00:35:22.580
I am Mr. Christos' personal solicitor.

00:35:23.260 --> 00:35:24.700
This is Mr. Yosh.

00:35:25.010 --> 00:35:27.050
He also is employed by Mr. Christos.

00:35:27.350 --> 00:35:29.490
Well, if there's anything I can do for Mr. Christos...

00:35:29.490 --> 00:35:29.850
Yes, quite.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.240
Mr. Christo is disturbed. Yes, disturbed.

00:35:35.080 --> 00:35:39.920
Word has reached him that a certain Harry Fabian is about to engage in the promotion of wrestling.

00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:47.580
It is Mr. Christo's opinion, sir, that this Mr. Fabian would find such a venture unprofitable.

00:35:48.520 --> 00:35:50.960
I can assure you that Mr. Christo need have no concern.

00:35:51.500 --> 00:35:55.180
Tonight, Mr. Fabian is pleased to regard himself as a great sports promoter.

00:35:55.670 --> 00:35:57.990
Tomorrow, he will undoubtedly own Coffin Garden.

00:35:58.540 --> 00:35:59.640
He is given to these...

00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:05.120
Mr. Christo has found it necessary to leave for Liverpool on business.

00:36:05.910 --> 00:36:10.950
Therefore, it might prove fruitful if Mr. Fabian called on me for a brief talk.

00:36:12.030 --> 00:36:14.170
Would you give him my card, sir?

00:36:15.330 --> 00:36:15.990
It'll be delighted.

00:36:17.190 --> 00:36:19.000
Thank you. Good night.

00:37:04.410 --> 00:37:08.390
Give me to get inside, and then go and get his $200, could you?

00:37:09.110 --> 00:37:11.810
Meet me tomorrow before lunch outside Bagrags.

00:37:11.890 --> 00:37:13.090
Bring me the $350.

00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:17.430
That leaves $50 for you to start your little wrestling stunt.

00:37:33.610 --> 00:37:34.830
How's it in there, dearie?

00:37:35.270 --> 00:37:37.290
How many times have I told you not to eat down here?

00:37:37.490 --> 00:37:40.110
You drop that swill and it brings mice. Clean it up and get up.

00:37:41.070 --> 00:37:41.930
Yes, my love.

00:37:46.580 --> 00:37:46.840
Get up.

00:37:47.350 --> 00:37:47.790
Come here.

00:37:49.140 --> 00:37:51.840
Oh, I'm just dead beat, Pet. I had a bit of a headache, so I walked it off.

00:37:51.880 --> 00:37:52.780
I want to talk to you.

00:37:53.210 --> 00:37:55.690
Oh, in the morning, Pet. Didn't we do well tonight, though?

00:37:55.870 --> 00:37:56.070
Now.

00:38:11.580 --> 00:38:16.540
I've been thinking, Helen. I'm a rich man. Richer than you know.

00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:25.110
I want to clear out. Sell this place. Get rid of everything. Just travel.

00:38:26.150 --> 00:38:29.880
Enjoy ourselves. See a bit of the world. Bermuda.

00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:30.430
Jamaica.

00:38:31.450 --> 00:38:32.630
Sounds exciting, Pip.

00:38:33.010 --> 00:38:35.710
But somehow I'm not in the mood for a holiday just now.

00:38:39.710 --> 00:38:39.910
Phil!

00:38:45.290 --> 00:38:46.310
Two hundred quid, Phil.

00:38:46.470 --> 00:38:48.480
Get on your desk.

00:38:49.460 --> 00:38:49.620
Catch it.

00:38:51.250 --> 00:38:52.470
Didn't think I could do it, did you?

00:38:52.900 --> 00:38:54.400
Didn't think I could raise two bob.

00:38:55.460 --> 00:38:56.360
It is, two hundred.

00:38:57.400 --> 00:38:58.180
This is it, Phil.

00:38:59.060 --> 00:38:59.960
Put up your money, your...

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:05.450
my partner. I'll play it square. I'll play it fair and square right down the line. And

00:39:05.450 --> 00:39:11.580
watch our 400 quid grow, Phil. Wrestling is just the beginning. Later on, we'll branch

00:39:11.580 --> 00:39:17.410
out. You'll be proud of me. You'll be proud to say, Harry Fabian? Why, he's my partner.

00:39:18.120 --> 00:39:21.770
Yes, sir. I'll say the word, Phil. You in or out.

00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:27.290
Really, didn't you? Didn't you have it?

00:39:28.430 --> 00:39:28.990
There it is.

00:39:32.490 --> 00:39:41.600
Yes, I must admit, I have underestimated you.

00:39:42.200 --> 00:39:45.610
Oh, that's all right, Phil. No hard feelings.

00:39:47.980 --> 00:39:48.700
Thank you, Harry.

00:39:50.640 --> 00:39:53.120
Yes, you have ideas, very smart ideas.

00:39:54.740 --> 00:39:57.200
There's no telling how far this will take you.

00:40:00.120 --> 00:40:04.410
I shall be happy to bank. Very happy indeed.

00:40:07.120 --> 00:40:07.980
Two hundred pounds.

00:40:10.590 --> 00:40:11.390
And two make four.

00:40:12.740 --> 00:40:14.080
Honored to be your partner.

00:40:14.320 --> 00:40:15.880
Fine, fine. You won't regret it, Phil.

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:17.540
I'm sure I shall, dear boy.

00:40:18.140 --> 00:40:21.020
Well, I'll be in touch with you, partner.

00:40:22.680 --> 00:40:27.760
Well, Harry, your asylum partner, for private reasons.

00:40:28.750 --> 00:40:29.970
I prefer the business to...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:39.490
be in your name. Oh, just my name? Yes. Now, remember, nobody must know about my connection

00:40:40.700 --> 00:40:51.370
for private businesses to be in your name. Well, all right, Phil. That's the way you want it. That's

00:40:51.370 --> 00:40:52.270
the way I want it.

00:41:11.860 --> 00:41:13.140
Hello, Strangler.

00:41:25.650 --> 00:41:29.320
Bad, bad, bad, bad new collapse.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.120
It's all you will do. Here, take my wrist like so.

00:41:34.090 --> 00:41:36.070
Hold it. Now try it.

00:41:41.950 --> 00:41:43.360
You go.

00:41:44.320 --> 00:41:45.080
I have ticket.

00:41:45.700 --> 00:41:48.640
Get out. This place is for wrestlers.

00:41:49.090 --> 00:41:52.420
I pay half-crown and I have ticket. If I pay my money, I can come in.

00:41:54.980 --> 00:41:59.260
There's your money. Now please leave.

00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:01.700
Go on, go on, we're busy.

00:42:14.670 --> 00:42:17.280
Charlie, don't ever let him in again.

00:42:18.070 --> 00:42:20.330
I told you to keep all that Crystal gang out of here.

00:42:20.610 --> 00:42:21.070
Yes, sir.

00:42:21.760 --> 00:42:23.260
All right, boys, let's get back to work.

00:42:23.380 --> 00:42:23.980
Let's get on with it.

00:42:24.060 --> 00:42:25.580
Come on, Nicholas, better have a rub.

00:42:25.700 --> 00:42:26.240
You're getting cool.

00:42:27.220 --> 00:42:27.660
That's it.

00:42:27.740 --> 00:42:28.600
Bend your backs, boys.

00:42:28.740 --> 00:42:29.400
Bend your backs.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:30.420
How are you, beauty?

00:42:30.900 --> 00:42:31.240
Yes.

00:42:32.040 --> 00:42:32.820
Right there, son.

00:42:33.240 --> 00:42:33.540
Thank you.

00:42:34.060 --> 00:42:36.800
Oh, sir.

00:42:37.380 --> 00:42:40.230
Thank you.

00:42:43.120 --> 00:42:43.340
Boy.

00:42:44.120 --> 00:42:44.560
Yes, sir.

00:42:45.100 --> 00:42:45.960
There you are, son.

00:42:47.250 --> 00:42:48.370
Thank you, sir.

00:43:09.930 --> 00:43:11.710
Just a moment. This is the pocket you made.

00:43:12.070 --> 00:43:13.170
I've got my orders.

00:43:13.490 --> 00:43:24.680
You will introduce us. Mr. Fabian? Mr. Christo?

00:43:24.890 --> 00:43:26.980
Yes, I... How do you do?

00:43:27.620 --> 00:43:29.400
I have here the copy of a contract.

00:43:30.250 --> 00:43:33.540
I've read it with great interest. The choker's going to read it to you.

00:43:34.520 --> 00:43:39.140
Agreed. Trans Arena Limited agrees to let to Harry Fabian...

00:43:39.140 --> 00:43:40.820
Oh, that is you, Harry Fabian.

00:43:41.020 --> 00:43:44.970
...the facilities of its arena for the purpose of exhibiting a wrestling match...

00:43:44.970 --> 00:43:47.950
...on June the 15th of the above-dated year...

00:43:48.100 --> 00:43:53.470
...when said Harry Fabian will present one Nicholas versus Svensson the Viking.

00:43:53.820 --> 00:43:56.900
June the 15th. That's four days from now.

00:43:58.200 --> 00:43:59.960
It would seem that I've returned to London with...

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:01.360
...without too many days to spare.

00:44:02.180 --> 00:44:04.600
It is further agreed that said Harry Fabian...

00:44:04.600 --> 00:44:06.420
...will make to Strand Arena Limited...

00:44:06.420 --> 00:44:08.120
...the final payment of £100...

00:44:08.120 --> 00:44:10.600
...no later than three days before the said exhibition.

00:44:11.100 --> 00:44:13.390
Namely, June 12th of about 80 years.

00:44:14.120 --> 00:44:14.460
It is...

00:44:14.640 --> 00:44:16.740
Yes, Nicholas versus Svensson.

00:44:16.840 --> 00:44:18.180
Fine boys, fine boys.

00:44:18.300 --> 00:44:19.780
I expect a big crowd.

00:44:20.280 --> 00:44:21.740
Oh, it's nothing like your stuff.

00:44:21.900 --> 00:44:23.840
It's real Greco-Roman wrestling.

00:44:24.580 --> 00:44:26.580
I'd be honoured, Mr. Christo, if you came...

00:44:29.640 --> 00:44:29.880
Go.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.940
Go away, Mr. Fabian. Go to Montreal, which is in Canada.

00:44:34.390 --> 00:44:36.930
There you can promote wrestling. In London, you cannot.

00:44:37.970 --> 00:44:39.410
I say it, Mr. Fabian.

00:44:40.920 --> 00:44:44.450
Then I suggest you say it to my partner.

00:44:55.000 --> 00:44:59.970
Mr. Christo? My partner. Mr. Christo has made an inter...

00:45:00.960 --> 00:45:05.260
That we go to Montreal because we can't promote wrestling in London.

00:45:08.120 --> 00:45:11.950
What do you think, Gregorius? Mr. Christos says there's no room for you in London.

00:45:12.510 --> 00:45:13.890
Papa, you did not go home.

00:45:14.620 --> 00:45:15.560
What do you want?

00:45:16.950 --> 00:45:19.690
I want to talk to you. Now.

00:45:20.530 --> 00:45:22.450
I have nothing to hear from you.

00:45:22.740 --> 00:45:27.270
I beg you to listen. You must not get mixed up with this club tout.

00:45:27.610 --> 00:45:29.950
If you would say something good about Mr.

00:45:31.130 --> 00:45:32.270
Then I worry.

00:45:32.530 --> 00:45:35.170
Papa, please, everybody in London knows what he is.

00:45:35.230 --> 00:45:37.750
He'll swindle you, he'll cheat you, he'll break your heart.

00:45:38.200 --> 00:45:42.220
You have break my heart. He is my partner and my friend.

00:45:43.030 --> 00:45:44.730
Stay away from him, my son.

00:45:45.550 --> 00:45:48.130
When you lift your hand to him, you strike me.

00:46:03.800 --> 00:46:06.680
You're very sharp, Mr. Fabian. You've done a very sharp thing.

00:46:07.710 --> 00:46:10.010
Maybe even sharp enough to cut your throat.

00:46:11.380 --> 00:46:13.580
Made my father believe in you, but I know you.

00:46:14.580 --> 00:46:17.480
Born a hustler, you will die a hustler.

00:46:19.830 --> 00:46:24.960
All right. You promised him clean wrestling. Give him clean wrestling.

00:46:26.180 --> 00:46:28.700
Do not betray that wonderful old man.

00:46:55.790 --> 00:46:56.710
Good afternoon, Mr. Fabian.

00:46:59.220 --> 00:46:59.480
Good afternoon.

00:47:00.190 --> 00:47:03.170
I am Mr. Hoskins, the manager of the Royal Tudor Hotel.

00:47:03.700 --> 00:47:05.920
Oh, yes. Yes, Mr. Hoskins.

00:47:06.480 --> 00:47:09.780
I'm very glad you dropped it. I've been meaning to speak to you about...

00:47:09.780 --> 00:47:12.320
Indeed. I was rather under the impression that you've been deliberately avoiding me.

00:47:12.680 --> 00:47:15.220
My secretary has tried to reach you seven times on the telephone.

00:47:15.400 --> 00:47:17.100
Oh, well, that's very easy to explain, Mr. Hoskins.

00:47:17.100 --> 00:47:20.160
I must confess I find this whole situation a trifle bizarre.

00:47:20.820 --> 00:47:22.520
Well, it's really very simple, Mr. Hoskins.

00:47:22.520 --> 00:47:23.960
Please have the courtesy to hear me out, sir.

00:47:26.590 --> 00:47:29.260
Now, I do not quite understand how you managed it.

00:47:29.460 --> 00:47:29.960
I suppose...

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:36.050
I never shall, but you have succeeded in obtaining from my inefficient staff two suites, two, mark you.

00:47:36.950 --> 00:47:43.740
For yourself, for Mr. Gregorius, and for an individual who seems to bear no name other than Nicholas.

00:47:43.920 --> 00:47:44.880
Oh, yes, yes. Well, you see, my...

00:47:44.880 --> 00:47:49.570
You've occupied these rooms for three weeks now, and to date, not one penny piece has been paid.

00:47:49.730 --> 00:47:50.770
Well, you see, Mr. Haskins, my solicitor...

00:47:50.770 --> 00:47:57.480
You will settle this bill, Mr. Fabian, for 287 pounds six and threepence in its entirety and in cash,

00:47:58.420 --> 00:47:59.980
or else I shall be forced to turn you...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:06.330
and your associates out of your rooms at once and then i shall return me out why you measly eight

00:48:06.330 --> 00:48:10.570
quid a week bookkeeper do you know who i just threw out of here do you know who i am yes you

00:48:11.100 --> 00:48:29.890
are a cheap spiv please sir listen i've got to do all this on d quid look

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:34.100
Just look at this gym. You'll get your money, every penny of it.

00:48:35.740 --> 00:48:40.000
All my life, Mr. Hoskins, I've fought and I've waited for a chance to be someone.

00:48:41.390 --> 00:48:43.940
And now I'm almost there. I'm doing it.

00:48:45.240 --> 00:48:47.680
But if you throw us out of the hotel, I'll lose my partner.

00:48:49.760 --> 00:48:54.560
I'll lose everything. Please, sir, I beg you.

00:48:55.750 --> 00:48:59.950
Just give me this one break and I promise you, I promise you on my life...

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.980
I am not one of my inefficient staff.

00:49:04.290 --> 00:49:05.950
Unless that money is paid into my office today,

00:49:06.440 --> 00:49:09.020
I shall impound your belongings and Mr. Gregorius's.

00:49:09.520 --> 00:49:10.680
I shall then inform the police,

00:49:10.960 --> 00:49:14.580
and I rather fancy you'll find yourself in slightly less comfortable quarters.

00:49:24.630 --> 00:49:26.890
Yes, yes, all right. He's still asleep.

00:49:27.400 --> 00:49:29.840
Great stroke of luck. My connection came through.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:30.880
You've got your license.

00:49:31.820 --> 00:49:35.100
Are you absolutely sure?

00:49:35.740 --> 00:49:37.660
It's going to cost you something, though. It wasn't easy to get.

00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:39.120
Oh, I knew it.

00:49:39.260 --> 00:49:41.360
If there's anybody in London who could do it, it'd be you.

00:49:41.740 --> 00:49:43.120
I'll bring the license to you in about...

00:49:43.120 --> 00:49:45.260
No, no. Stay where you are. I'll meet you there.

00:49:45.460 --> 00:49:50.320
No, no, no. That won't be necessary. You see, I haven't got it yet.

00:49:50.840 --> 00:49:52.060
But you just said you had it, didn't you?

00:49:52.280 --> 00:49:54.830
What are you up to, Harry? Am I going to meet you there or not?

00:49:55.170 --> 00:49:59.110
Well, all right, all right. I'll meet you at the court at 3 o'clock.

00:50:00.510 --> 00:50:02.600
No. No, Helen. Make it four o'clock.

00:50:03.470 --> 00:50:06.060
All right. But please don't keep me waiting, Harry.

00:50:06.570 --> 00:50:08.210
I'll be there at four o'clock. Goodbye.

00:50:38.670 --> 00:50:43.310
Mr. Noceros, you puzzle me. You confuse me.

00:50:44.240 --> 00:50:47.180
How is it possible that you want to invest in Christo's enterprises

00:50:47.180 --> 00:50:49.400
and at the same time you're backing Harry Fabian?

00:50:50.260 --> 00:50:51.300
I don't quite understand.

00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:54.320
I know that you are Fabian's backer. Now let's have that clear.

00:50:58.280 --> 00:50:59.480
Now what do you really want?

00:51:03.480 --> 00:51:05.120
Harry Fabian is in my way.

00:51:05.400 --> 00:51:07.960
Harry Fabian is in my way because of you.

00:51:08.500 --> 00:51:09.440
You fed him money.

00:51:09.540 --> 00:51:13.190
I can withdraw that money, and then you will be free to deal with him.

00:51:13.750 --> 00:51:16.050
You missed the point, Mr. Noseros.

00:51:16.510 --> 00:51:18.290
It isn't your money that keeps him alive.

00:51:19.400 --> 00:51:20.960
Harry Fabian is not a competitor,

00:51:22.380 --> 00:51:25.420
as long as he keeps his promise to promote only Greco-Roman wrestling.

00:51:25.760 --> 00:51:27.160
His business failure is certain.

00:51:27.700 --> 00:51:29.960
The public simply won't buy it, but the point is...

00:51:30.540 --> 00:51:33.900
My father would still believe that Harry Fabian is an honorable man.

00:51:34.270 --> 00:51:37.100
And I can't touch him. He's unpunished.

00:51:37.450 --> 00:51:40.370
And I'm not satisfied merely to see him become a hustler once again.

00:51:42.820 --> 00:51:43.500
Neither am I.

00:51:43.900 --> 00:51:46.220
Just a minute, Mr. Noseros. We haven't finished.

00:51:46.960 --> 00:51:48.620
I'll deliver Fabian to you.

00:51:49.920 --> 00:51:54.080
Your father shall learn that Harry Fabian is not an honorable man.

00:52:01.980 --> 00:52:05.720
Hello, Phil. Sorry to be late. So many things to take care of.

00:52:05.900 --> 00:52:07.520
Business, business, business.

00:52:08.020 --> 00:52:09.280
Why'd you ask me to meet you here?

00:52:09.580 --> 00:52:11.420
I'm afraid of Christo. You're not.

00:52:11.680 --> 00:52:14.530
You bet I'm not. He came to the gym this morning.

00:52:14.650 --> 00:52:17.990
You know what he said? Go to Montreal, which is in Canada.

00:52:18.650 --> 00:52:21.770
You know what I did? Had the bouncer tossing down the stairs.

00:52:22.010 --> 00:52:23.410
He crawled like a sewer rat.

00:52:23.530 --> 00:52:24.130
I'm sure.

00:52:24.410 --> 00:52:26.110
Now, there's just one thing more to settle, Phil.

00:52:26.210 --> 00:52:29.230
The hundred quid for the final payment of the arena. We're all set.

00:52:29.410 --> 00:52:29.970
Had it.

00:52:30.020 --> 00:52:34.480
I've brought you here to tell you that I'm withdrawing from our partnership.

00:52:35.030 --> 00:52:35.270
What?

00:52:35.840 --> 00:52:39.220
Well, I'm advised that your kind of wrestling can't succeed.

00:52:39.480 --> 00:52:42.170
This Grinco-Roman won't draw fly.

00:52:42.620 --> 00:52:45.280
But you can't back out now. You've invested a lot of money.

00:52:45.610 --> 00:52:47.970
I'm sorry. I'll take the loss, and that's final.

00:52:52.770 --> 00:52:56.280
Bill, wait! Bill! Bill, wait!

00:52:56.920 --> 00:52:59.720
Why are you backing out? Everything's in the palm of my hand. Why?

00:53:00.090 --> 00:53:01.830
I refuse to throw good money out to bed.

00:53:01.950 --> 00:53:03.510
But you know what this means to me, Phil.

00:53:04.110 --> 00:53:06.760
Harry, Harry, this is my last word on the subject.

00:53:07.420 --> 00:53:09.500
Get a box office attraction, a big name.

00:53:09.720 --> 00:53:10.660
Then you'll get the money.

00:53:11.660 --> 00:53:12.260
What do you mean?

00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:14.180
Well, I know nothing about wrestling,

00:53:14.360 --> 00:53:16.400
but I'm told there are men who are big draw.

00:53:17.210 --> 00:53:19.720
Men like, for instance, the strangler.

00:53:20.100 --> 00:53:23.910
But I can't. Gregorius would leave me.

00:53:24.380 --> 00:53:25.960
If you don't, then I'm forced to leave you.

00:53:26.120 --> 00:53:27.000
And then will I.

00:53:28.260 --> 00:53:29.980
Now, as I see it, Harry, you're only...

00:53:30.120 --> 00:53:35.050
course is to keep moving right ahead go on get the strangler that's your first problem and then

00:53:35.050 --> 00:53:40.280
i'm sure you'll have no difficulty in persuading any wrestler to beat him seems to me you have no

00:53:40.280 --> 00:53:50.870
alternative have you i can do it i can do it i'll do it but will you give me the money to get the

00:53:50.870 --> 00:53:56.250
strangler of course i will i'll back you without a limit i consider it a sound investment dear boy

00:53:56.250 --> 00:53:56.810
all right

00:54:07.900 --> 00:54:21.180
Another the same gin for me. Hello, beer. What's a good word?

00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:26.060
Well, hello to you. Hey, words all over town that you made Christo turn tail.

00:54:26.340 --> 00:54:29.200
How'd you do it? Brains, chum, brains and guts.

00:54:30.090 --> 00:54:36.430
stopping you now, eh, Harry? Never was. Where's the strangler? Join Madame La Poche's circus for dinner.

