01:19:41.950 --> 01:19:47.600
Helen, believe me. Believe me. There's no future with Fabian.

01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:51.140
I'll make one. I know Fabian, and I'll control him.

01:19:54.860 --> 01:19:59.190
I've been good to you. I've done everything for you.

01:20:01.756 --> 01:20:02.316
I love you.

01:20:02.528 --> 01:20:05.688
Oh, for goodness sake, Phil, at least say goodbye like a man.

01:21:01.490 --> 01:21:02.450
Good night, Constable.

01:21:10.930 --> 01:21:12.110
Oh, Constable, there you are.

01:21:13.120 --> 01:21:15.260
My name is Reeves. I'm with that construction crew.

01:21:15.440 --> 01:21:15.740
Oh, yeah?

01:21:15.840 --> 01:21:19.520
We're putting up some land platforms so we can load a few lorries with cement from the exhibition site.

01:21:19.700 --> 01:21:21.060
I suppose you've got permission of the air, sir?

01:21:21.280 --> 01:21:23.360
Oh, yes, yes. The superintendent's taking care of all that.

01:21:23.820 --> 01:21:25.460
You see, I had in mind to take our platform...

01:21:25.460 --> 01:21:27.180
Look at those chaps in the car.

01:21:27.320 --> 01:21:27.740
They're not with you?

01:21:27.900 --> 01:21:28.860
No, they're not with our company.

01:21:29.290 --> 01:21:29.850
Might be lawyer.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:31.000
I never were with them.

01:21:31.000 --> 01:21:32.000
You have to do no harm.

01:21:32.000 --> 01:21:33.000
This time of night, you never know.

01:21:33.000 --> 01:21:34.000
That's right, sir.

01:21:34.412 --> 01:21:35.412
May I help you, gentlemen?

01:21:35.412 --> 01:21:38.412
Ah, well, we seem to be lost. We've been driving around and around.

01:21:38.956 --> 01:21:40.536
Did you tell me how to get to York Road?

01:21:40.536 --> 01:21:42.216
About 40 yards on the other side there.

01:22:18.652 --> 01:22:19.152
Shut the-

01:24:13.790 --> 01:24:15.270
Where do you know you? Do you belong here?

01:24:16.280 --> 01:24:16.960
Where's Folly?

01:24:17.270 --> 01:24:17.590
Who?

01:24:17.970 --> 01:24:20.040
Folly, the engineer from the office.

01:24:20.320 --> 01:24:21.640
Oh, I don't know.

01:24:22.460 --> 01:24:23.140
Where's the Folly?

01:24:23.280 --> 01:24:24.600
Up in the shack, sir.

01:24:24.800 --> 01:24:25.560
Up in the shack.

01:24:43.760 --> 01:24:44.320
Figler, here.

01:24:47.060 --> 01:24:47.380
Figler?

01:24:48.710 --> 01:24:51.260
Hey, listen, I need help.

01:24:52.320 --> 01:24:53.660
A place to hide till I can get away.

01:24:54.420 --> 01:24:54.740
Yes.

01:24:55.000 --> 01:24:55.740
Yes, I know, Harry.

01:24:56.690 --> 01:24:57.230
I heard.

01:24:57.800 --> 01:24:58.240
Where are you?

01:24:58.360 --> 01:24:59.580
It's only a few minutes away.

01:25:00.440 --> 01:25:02.440
Please, Fiddler, please, let me come.

01:25:02.920 --> 01:25:04.780
Yeah, sure. Come right away, Harry boy.

01:25:05.360 --> 01:25:06.140
You'll be safe here.

01:25:07.090 --> 01:25:07.710
Thanks, Fiddler.

01:25:22.410 --> 01:25:25.170
Fiddler here. Let me talk to Mr. Christo.

01:25:26.540 --> 01:25:29.360
Find him. Tell him to phone me at once. Urgent.

01:25:30.670 --> 01:25:32.950
No, no, no. I don't trust nobody.

01:25:33.130 --> 01:25:35.550
I ain't doing business with nobody but Mr. Christo himself.

01:25:36.550 --> 01:25:37.770
Not for 1,000 quid, I ain't.

01:25:56.310 --> 01:25:56.690
Tegli.

01:26:00.890 --> 01:26:03.090
Harry, didn't expect you so quick.

01:26:03.340 --> 01:26:08.170
Thanks, sir. Sorry.

01:26:09.090 --> 01:26:13.290
You didn't. I have some work to do.

01:26:14.060 --> 01:26:17.710
You're a poor chap. Deadbeat.

01:26:19.540 --> 01:26:22.450
Deadbeat, ain't you? Water's nearly boiling.

01:26:23.190 --> 01:26:26.310
Soon have some tea. You need a little bit of life in you.

01:26:27.100 --> 01:26:29.510
And then you can go upstairs and rest.

01:26:30.190 --> 01:26:30.530
Thanks.

01:26:32.330 --> 01:26:33.930
Always glad to help a friend.

01:26:35.560 --> 01:26:37.460
Hard on this instrument, Burgess.

01:26:39.500 --> 01:26:41.380
You don't give it the care it wants, eh?

01:26:42.490 --> 01:26:49.290
That's right. Just lay there and rest. Just lay there and rest.

01:26:51.200 --> 01:26:54.720
Keep his glass filled. There'll be a waiter at your elbow all the time.

01:26:55.840 --> 01:26:58.220
Oh, good evening, officer.

01:26:59.100 --> 01:26:59.640
Good evening, ma'am.

01:27:01.810 --> 01:27:06.390
I have this place listed as being struck off for another year and I've had no word from the station.

01:27:06.670 --> 01:27:12.940
You will have. Here. This your regular bee?

01:27:14.330 --> 01:27:17.440
I hope so, ma'am. Just finished training school last month.

01:27:17.680 --> 01:27:20.360
Well, good for you. Let's have a drink to celebrate it.

01:27:20.460 --> 01:27:22.860
I'm sorry, ma'am. A police constable on duty is not permitted to...

01:27:22.860 --> 01:27:25.860
Oh, come on. You can't be breaking many rules with a little ginger ale.

01:27:26.570 --> 01:27:29.690
We're opening here on Saturday night. You certainly can't refuse to wish me luck.

01:27:30.090 --> 01:27:40.820
thank you ma'am all the best well everything seems to be in order i'll just make a note of

01:27:40.820 --> 01:27:53.680
the serial number where did you obtain this license ma'am i'm afraid this is not in order

01:27:53.680 --> 01:27:57.480
i shall have to take it up and deliver it to the authorities of bow street

01:28:01.180 --> 01:28:03.500
I'm sure you'll be able to explain everything at the police court.

01:28:03.680 --> 01:28:06.440
I'm sorry, ma'am.

01:28:08.240 --> 01:28:08.540
Good night.

01:29:03.480 --> 01:29:11.980
You said I'd come back. Oh, forgive me, Phil. I was out of my mind. I didn't mean those things.

01:29:12.320 --> 01:29:17.870
Take me back, Phil. I'll be good to you. I'll do everything for you. I'll look after you.

01:29:20.360 --> 01:29:29.140
Let's make that be wonderful. Phil, take me back. Please take me back.

01:29:31.370 --> 01:29:32.810
Bill, give me another chance.

01:29:33.550 --> 01:29:40.650
Good as new.

01:29:42.630 --> 01:29:43.370
Feel all right now.

01:29:44.260 --> 01:29:44.860
Think I'll move.

01:29:45.280 --> 01:29:46.270
Where? Why?

01:29:46.450 --> 01:29:47.850
It's getting light. I gotta get out of London.

01:29:48.210 --> 01:29:48.910
I'll use a back way.

01:29:49.350 --> 01:29:50.170
You're crazy, Harry.

01:29:50.430 --> 01:29:50.850
Not tonight.

01:29:51.340 --> 01:29:52.740
Tonight, the old underworld's after you.

01:29:53.420 --> 01:29:54.100
Stay here.

01:29:54.540 --> 01:29:55.380
You're safe, are you?

01:29:55.560 --> 01:29:56.140
No, thanks.

01:29:56.300 --> 01:29:57.500
One of your beggars will pop in.

01:29:57.600 --> 01:29:58.140
It'll be all over.

01:29:58.180 --> 01:29:58.720
Oh, let him see you.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:02.060
You won't let him in. I'll lock the door.

01:30:03.940 --> 01:30:07.850
That's right. I'll lock the door. Then no one will come in.

01:30:10.520 --> 01:30:14.260
What do I mean, Harry? Stay here. Go upstairs.

01:30:15.120 --> 01:30:16.160
I'll nip out and have a look round.

01:30:16.590 --> 01:30:19.730
And if I see anybody, I'll tip you off. I'll come and tell you.

01:30:23.270 --> 01:30:27.180
Okay, Harry. You're right. One of my beggars might come in.

01:30:28.210 --> 01:30:29.170
I'll nip out and get me lorry.

01:30:30.760 --> 01:30:31.760
I lied you in the back.

01:30:50.490 --> 01:30:51.310
Yes, Mrs. Figgler.

01:30:52.960 --> 01:30:53.340
Yes.

01:30:53.860 --> 01:30:54.440
Yes, I did.

01:30:55.400 --> 01:30:56.600
No, I can't.

01:30:57.950 --> 01:30:58.510
I can't.

01:31:00.640 --> 01:31:07.080
Yes, of course I do. Yes, sir. That would be a bit difficult.

01:31:09.950 --> 01:31:12.660
Yes. Yes. Right on the premises.

01:31:19.450 --> 01:31:20.650
How much are you selling?

01:31:22.220 --> 01:31:22.740
How are you?

01:32:42.860 --> 01:32:43.380
Who's there?

01:32:49.300 --> 01:32:49.620
Harry.

01:32:53.850 --> 01:32:55.750
It's no good coming to me.

01:32:56.440 --> 01:32:57.640
I can't help you.

01:32:58.040 --> 01:32:59.240
Nobody can help you.

01:33:00.380 --> 01:33:06.210
I don't want any help. I just want to sit down and rest.

01:33:07.850 --> 01:33:10.980
I can't run anymore.

01:33:12.520 --> 01:33:16.760
Come on in. You're a sorry sight. Come on.

01:33:24.690 --> 01:33:28.300
Much good. I know the riverfront's alive.

01:33:29.210 --> 01:33:29.970
Just alive.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:32.000
Are you hungry?

01:33:32.280 --> 01:33:32.540
No.

01:33:42.090 --> 01:33:42.310
And?

01:33:42.950 --> 01:33:43.650
Yes, Daddy.

01:33:45.760 --> 01:33:47.640
All my life I've been running.

01:33:49.720 --> 01:33:55.440
Welfare officers, thugs, father.

01:34:00.160 --> 01:34:11.100
Then, they're undead.

01:34:21.260 --> 01:34:27.020
Said, you've got it all, but you're a dead man.

01:34:31.530 --> 01:34:32.610
Mary said it too.

01:34:37.340 --> 01:34:54.360
Said, you're killing me and you're killing your son of love.

01:35:05.820 --> 01:35:06.280
on the side.

01:35:34.830 --> 01:35:35.730
I've got a close stance.

01:36:06.010 --> 01:36:07.270
I've been looking for you every way.

01:36:08.250 --> 01:36:08.610
Mary.

01:36:11.760 --> 01:36:13.080
You've got to get out of London, Harry.

01:36:15.870 --> 01:36:16.590
I've got some money for you.

01:36:18.380 --> 01:36:19.260
Don't be kind.

01:36:25.260 --> 01:36:26.700
It was all my fault, Harry.

01:36:29.080 --> 01:36:29.980
I didn't know how to help.

01:36:33.290 --> 01:36:35.430
No woman could love anybody like I loved you.

01:36:38.660 --> 01:36:41.150
You kept me shut out from so much.

01:36:41.270 --> 01:36:45.840
I couldn't keep up with you.

01:37:01.050 --> 01:37:04.480
You could have been anything, anything.

01:37:07.780 --> 01:37:10.760
You had ambition.

01:37:13.220 --> 01:37:23.100
You worked harder than any ten men think.

01:37:30.920 --> 01:37:32.040
Listen, I've got an idea.

01:37:32.800 --> 01:37:34.800
Harry Fabian's not through yet.

01:37:35.560 --> 01:37:38.140
I always promised you a life of ease and plenty, didn't I?

01:37:38.500 --> 01:37:39.820
Well, I can still make you.

01:37:40.300 --> 01:37:42.180
The money I took from you, that's chicken.

01:37:42.360 --> 01:37:43.380
Now listen, pay attention.

01:37:43.930 --> 01:37:47.190
There's a reward for my head, a thousand pounds, a thousand pounds.

01:37:47.350 --> 01:37:48.010
Oh, Harry, don't go.

01:37:48.010 --> 01:37:48.910
Now, out you go on the bridge.

01:37:49.130 --> 01:37:50.710
Christo's there, but he doesn't know where I am.

01:37:50.850 --> 01:37:51.290
Oh, Harry.

01:37:51.290 --> 01:37:53.890
You tell him where I am and it's a thousand quid for you.

01:37:53.890 --> 01:37:54.150
Oh, Harry.

01:37:54.650 --> 01:37:55.630
Somebody's got to collect.

01:37:55.990 --> 01:37:59.610
No, Mary, for the first time in my life, it's a foolproof idea.

01:37:59.750 --> 01:37:59.970
Don't you?

01:38:00.120 --> 01:38:00.380
See?

01:39:00.860 --> 01:39:07.070
Restore the blood money she cut my throat for you, pay her the double belt!
